"""Editorial question designs for traditional painting, street art, and sculpture."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


TRADITIONAL_PAINTING = """history_origins|A Painting Tradition's Early Record|What dated works document a named local form?|Separate earliest surviving object from absolute origin.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Painting in Context|What does one work reveal and what is exceptional?|Check maker, purpose, audience, technique, and provenance.
hidden_stories|Painters and Preparers|Whose grinding, surface making, teaching, and repair are omitted?|Credit collaborative labor and consented accounts.
beginner_explainers|Reading One Painting Form|How do surface, pigment, motif, and use fit together?|Name community and setting; ask practitioners about meaning.
advanced_concepts|Variation Within a Tradition|How do painters change form without losing continuity?|Compare dated works and maker explanations.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Attribution|Which evidence might identify the painter or workshop?|Compare provenance, materials, style, inscriptions, and limits.
technology_innovation|A Material or Reproduction Shift|How did a new pigment, surface, or print process alter work?|Test cost, durability, access, and maker control.
people_personalities|A Painter-Teacher's Contribution|How did one artist pass on techniques?|Trace students and work within the wider community.
major_events|A Collection or Market Turning Point|How did one documented event change making or ownership?|Use dated sales, exhibitions, laws, and maker accounts.
how_it_works|From Surface to Finished Work|Which choices shape one painting?|Observe preparation, drawing, pigment, layering, and finishing with consent.
rise_fall|Demand for a Painting Form|What explains a measured shift in production?|Check commissions, materials, markets, and survey coverage.
then_vs_now|A Form Across Generations|How did technique, patronage, and subject change?|Compare provenanced works and practitioner views.
future_developments|Supporting Living Painters|Which resources do makers prioritize?|Compare training, materials, fair pay, rights, and display.
myths_vs_facts|A Single Authentic Style?|What documented variations exist among makers and periods?|Avoid ranking one market-approved version as true.
documentary_stories|One Painting's Journey|How was it made, sold, displayed, or returned?|Trace custody and consented maker and owner accounts.
creative_brief|A Commission's Requirements|How did use, audience, site, and maker choice shape it?|Read the agreement and record permitted imagery.
materials_and_tools|Pigment and Surface Choice|Why use a specific binder, brush, or support?|Check provenance, properties, cost, and maker explanation.
process_breakdown|The Painter's Sequence|Which stages require revision or waiting?|Use consented workshop observation and dated notes.
composition_choice|Why This Arrangement|How do makers explain placement, scale, and color?|Attribute meanings and distinguish outside interpretation.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made This Work|How do family, assistants, patrons, and painter contribute?|Trace credit, pay, and decision rights.
adaptation_across_media|Painting to Print or Screen|What changes in scale, color, texture, and control?|Compare original and reproduction with rights context.
audience_reception|Two Viewers, Different Readings|How do local and gallery audiences interpret it?|Use varied accounts and explain context.
cultural_context|When an Image May Be Shown|Which customary or legal permissions matter?|Consult maker and custodians; respect restricted imagery.
preservation_restoration|Conserving a Used Painting|Which treatment protects material and meaning?|Compare condition, maker intent, use, and owner wishes.
rights_and_attribution|Reusing a Pattern|Who may reproduce motifs or sell derivatives?|Check maker permission, community claims, contract, and jurisdiction.
style_comparison|Two Works in One Tradition|Which differences reflect maker, purpose, or period?|Use provenanced examples and avoid simplistic regional labels.
creative_failure|A Material Problem Solved|What did the painter change when pigment or support failed?|Use consented records and distinguish defect from intentional effect.
field_visual_composition|A Close Reading of One Work|What do line, color, scale, and sequence actually show?|Start with observation, then attribute interpretations.
field_material_provenance|Where the Pigment Came From|Can supply and ownership be traced?|Use maker records, analysis, and uncertainty.
field_maker_technique|Technique in Practice|How does a named painter create a feature?|Observe with consent and credit their explanation.
field_conservation_problem|A Painting's Current Condition|What deterioration is visible and what caused it?|Use conservation assessment; avoid speculative treatment.
field_audience_context|The Work's Display Setting|How does a home, ritual, market, or museum change reception?|Compare access, labels, and maker wishes.
"""

STREET_ART = """history_origins|A City's Early Street-Art Record|What dated images or accounts show a local scene?|Distinguish earliest documentation from first work.
famous_examples|A Viral Mural Revisited|What does a famous wall mean in its neighborhood?|Compare artist intent, resident views, ownership, and tourism.
hidden_stories|Work Around the Wall|Who prepares, permits, photographs, cleans, or removes a piece?|Trace labor and institutional roles.
beginner_explainers|Reading Street Art in Place|How do image, surface, location, and legality shape meaning?|Name artist or anonymous status, site, date, and context.
advanced_concepts|Public Art and Property|Who controls an image on a privately owned public-facing wall?|Examine permission, rights, maintenance, and jurisdiction.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Who Made an Unsigned Work|Which attribution evidence is credible?|Compare artist statements, dated images, technique, and uncertainty.
technology_innovation|A Street Work Goes Online|How did mapping or social media alter its audience?|Check credit, location exposure, copying, and local impact.
people_personalities|An Artist's Public Decision|Why did a named artist choose one site or collaboration?|Use consented interviews and dated proposals.
major_events|A Wall After Redevelopment|How did one project change the art and surrounding community?|Trace permits, removal, relocation, and resident response.
how_it_works|From Proposal to Wall|How does a permitted public artwork get made?|Trace artist, owner, community, materials, access, and maintenance.
rise_fall|A District's Changing Wall Count|Does a claimed boom reflect new work or better documentation?|Compare dated surveys, turnover, and definitions.
then_vs_now|One Wall Across Years|What happened to the image and its context?|Use dated photographs, repair records, and ownership changes.
future_developments|What Happens to a Temporary Work|Which choices do artist and community favor?|Compare repainting, documentation, removal, and consent.
myths_vs_facts|Street Art Always Unauthorized?|How do permissions and commissioning vary?|Check a named work's agreement and jurisdiction.
documentary_stories|One Mural's Life|How was it created, received, altered, and removed?|Build a dated record with artist and neighbor voices.
creative_brief|An Image for a Public Wall|Which site and audience constraints shape the commission?|Document artist aims, permissions, surface, access, and budget.
materials_and_tools|Paint on an Outdoor Surface|How do wall and pigment choices affect longevity?|Use artist and conservator evidence, not application instructions.
process_breakdown|Making a Permitted Mural|Which stages involve consultation and revision?|Trace proposal, agreement, preparation, execution, and care.
composition_choice|Image at Street Scale|How does viewing distance or movement shape composition?|Compare sketches, site photographs, and artist explanation.
collaborative_authorship|Who Owns the Idea|How do artist, assistants, residents, and sponsor influence the work?|Trace credit and decision rights.
adaptation_across_media|Wall to Photograph|What is lost when a site-specific image circulates online?|Compare scale, setting, crop, credit, and rights.
audience_reception|Neighbors and Visitors|How do local and tourist interpretations differ?|Seek varied consented views and note who is sampled.
cultural_context|Symbols on a Shared Wall|Which histories or sensitivities shape reception?|Consult affected communities and avoid imposing one reading.
preservation_restoration|Should a Wall Be Saved|When is fading or replacement part of the work?|Compare artist intent, owner rights, community wishes, and condition.
rights_and_attribution|Reproduction of a Mural|Who may photograph, sell, or alter its image?|Check artist, property, commissioning contract, and local law.
style_comparison|Two Works in One District|How do site and commissioning alter visual choices?|Compare dated works without equating all public images.
creative_failure|A Public Artwork Revised|What changed after consultation or material failure?|Use dated sketches and attributed accounts.
field_visual_composition|Reading a Wall in Place|How do sightline, scale, and neighboring signs shape it?|Observe lawfully and document date and viewpoint.
field_material_provenance|Materials of One Mural|Can paint, support, and funding be traced?|Use artist records and condition evidence.
field_maker_technique|Artist's Method and Intent|What can the artist say about choices visible on the wall?|Seek consent and avoid publishing restricted details.
field_conservation_problem|A Damaged Street Work|Which causes of change are documented?|Compare weather, overpainting, maintenance, and intentional revision.
field_audience_context|Who Encounters the Work|How do route, access, and neighborhood use shape audience?|Map public viewing without exposing private residents.
"""

SCULPTURE = """history_origins|How a Sculptural Form Emerged|What dated works and tools show one method's development?|Name place and period; avoid a single invention claim.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Sculpture Rechecked|What does the object show beyond its iconic image?|Examine scale, material, site, maker, and provenance.
hidden_stories|Fabricators and Installers|Whose labor made a sculpture possible?|Trace studio assistants, foundries, quarries, transport, and care.
beginner_explainers|Reading Sculpture in Space|How do mass, surface, material, and viewpoint work together?|Use one object in its actual setting.
advanced_concepts|Object, Site, and Audience|How does relocating a sculpture change meaning?|Compare original and current site, access, and interpretation.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Sculptural Attribution|Which evidence could distinguish maker, workshop, and later repair?|Check provenance, tool marks, materials, and archives.
technology_innovation|A New Fabrication Method|How did casting, scanning, or printing alter one practice?|Compare artist control, labor, finish, and cost.
people_personalities|A Sculptor's Collaboration|Which people influenced one major commission?|Use contracts, sketches, studio records, and credit.
major_events|A Monument Moved or Contested|How did one decision change a sculpture's public role?|Trace authority, consultation, site, and community response.
how_it_works|From Model to Installation|What stages turn an idea into a stable work?|Map maquette, material, fabrication, transport, installation, and maintenance.
rise_fall|A Material's Changing Use|Why did one sculptural material gain or lose favor?|Compare supply, price, technique, fashion, and conservation.
then_vs_now|One Work Over Time|How have surface, setting, and interpretation changed?|Use condition reports and dated photographs.
future_developments|The Sculpture's Next Home|Which choices affect continued access and care?|Compare funding, conservation, artist intent, and public use.
myths_vs_facts|Made by One Hand?|What did the credited artist and workshop each do?|Check contracts, process photos, and maker accounts.
documentary_stories|One Sculpture's Full Life|How was it made, owned, displayed, and repaired?|Build a dated provenance and conservation timeline.
creative_brief|A Sculpture for a Site|Which spatial, material, and audience needs shaped the commission?|Read brief, permits, artist proposal, and constraints.
materials_and_tools|Why This Material|How does stone, metal, wood, or found matter affect form?|Compare properties, sourcing, labor, and maintenance.
process_breakdown|Fabrication Decisions|Which stages changed the design?|Use models, workshop records, and maker testimony.
composition_choice|Form from Multiple Viewpoints|What changes as a viewer moves around the object?|Describe measured scale, sightlines, and artist explanation.
collaborative_authorship|The Studio and Foundry|How should fabricators and assistants be credited?|Trace roles, contracts, and attribution practice.
adaptation_across_media|Sculpture in a Photograph|What does a single image conceal?|Compare scale, texture, back, site, and movement.
audience_reception|Public Responses to One Work|How do viewers disagree about meaning or location?|Use dated, varied accounts and social context.
cultural_context|A Sculpture's Claims|Which historical or sacred meanings require contextual sources?|Consult custodians and distinguish artist intent from reception.
preservation_restoration|Repairing Material and Meaning|How should a damaged work be treated?|Compare condition, artist intent, owner, community, and reversibility.
rights_and_attribution|Control of a Public Sculpture|Who may move, alter, or reproduce it?|Check artist, owner, commission agreement, and jurisdiction.
style_comparison|Two Works, Different Construction|Which formal resemblance hides different methods?|Compare provenance, scale, material, and setting.
creative_failure|An Engineering Revision|What changed when a work could not be installed as planned?|Use dated design and installation records.
field_visual_composition|Sculpture on Site|How do height, approach, light, and surrounding uses shape it?|Observe legally from multiple viewpoints.
field_material_provenance|Where the Stone or Metal Came From|Can sourcing and fabrication be traced?|Check supplier, workshop, records, and gaps.
field_maker_technique|Marks of Making|What can surface and process records establish?|Compare artist and fabricator accounts with examination.
field_conservation_problem|A Deteriorating Surface|Which changes are damage versus intended aging?|Use conservator assessment and artist documentation.
field_audience_context|Who Can Encounter It|How does location affect accessibility and interpretation?|Compare opening hours, route, labels, and community use.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("258", "258_traditional_painting", TRADITIONAL_PAINTING,
                  "Named painting traditions through living makers, materials, provenance, permitted imagery, and display context.",
                  "provenanced dated works, material examination, maker records, conservation reports, and consented practitioner and audience accounts",
                  "Name community, maker, object, and period. Respect restricted imagery and reproduction rights; distinguish visual observation from attributed meaning.")
    revise_domain("259", "259_street_art", STREET_ART,
                  "Street art as site-specific public work shaped by artists, property, neighbors, law, and change over time.",
                  "dated site photographs and proposals, artist and property permissions, municipal records, conservation reports, and consented resident accounts",
                  "Name work, site, date, and jurisdiction. Verify rights and access; avoid exposing private residents or giving directions for unauthorized activity.")
    revise_domain("260", "260_sculpture", SCULPTURE,
                  "Sculpture through material, fabrication, site, collaborators, provenance, public reception, and care.",
                  "provenanced objects and models, studio and foundry records, commission contracts, site plans, conservation reports, and attributed community accounts",
                  "Name object, maker and collaborators, site, and date. Distinguish intent from reception and obtain rights information before reproducing or relocating work.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
